From: baseband lane
Subject: 0543 pandora_mpss: attach keeps step 7, because announcing is not loading

The first attach boot (ring 1795494675, kernel 0540) reached the desktop and ran steps 1,2,3 and 9,
then stopped at step 10:

  PANDORA MPSS: the modem has not made its FIFO (item 480)

Item 480 is the modem's own RX FIFO.  The modem creates it when the AP announces itself: the SMP2P
"master-kernel" item, the GLINK marks and the doorbells, which is step_our_item -- step 7.  Attach
mode skipped 4 through 8 in one condition, so the modem was never told that this side exists and had
no reason to build the FIFO the next step waits for.

Step 7 does not load or reset anything: it writes our own SMEM item and rings the doorbells.  The
steps that must stay skipped are the ones that put firmware in or start it -- 4 and 5 (INIT_IMAGE for
the DTB and the main image), 6 (the segment copy) and 8 (AUTH_AND_RESET).  Attach now skips exactly
{4,5,6,8} and keeps 7.

The comment above mp_attach said "steps 4..8 are skipped" and now says what is actually true, with the
ring that proved it.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index 3d2eda8..421350f 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -1685,10 +1685,14 @@ mp_steps_over(uint32_t done)
  * firmware" -- and to build the AP<->modem IPC and QRTR discovery on top of that.  Section 7.1
  * forbids triggering modem crash/SSR as an early debugging tool, which is what PAS_SHUTDOWN was.
  *
- * So steps 4..8 (INIT_IMAGE, MEM_SETUP, the segment copy, the SMP2P handshake that starts what we
- * copied, and AUTH_AND_RESET) are exactly the reload path and are skipped in attach mode.  What is
- * kept is what observes and what talks: the SMEM survey, the firmware identity, the mailbox, then
- * the GLINK queues, our side of the link, and QRTR.
+ * So steps 4..6 and 8 (INIT_IMAGE for the DTB and the main image, the segment copy, and the
+ * AUTH_AND_RESET that would start what we copied) are the reload path and are skipped in attach
+ * mode.  Step 7 stays: writing our SMP2P "master-kernel" item and the GLINK marks is how this side
+ * ANNOUNCES ITSELF to a modem that is already running -- it starts nothing, and without it the modem
+ * never creates the FIFO step 10 waits for (ring 1795494675: "the modem has not made its FIFO
+ * (item 480)", which is exactly what skipping the announcement produces).  What is kept is what
+ * observes and what talks: the SMEM survey, the firmware identity, the mailbox, our item, the GLINK
+ * queues, our side of the link, and QRTR.
  */
 static bool mp_attach;
 
@@ -1698,7 +1702,7 @@ mp_run_steps(void)
 	uint32_t done = 0;
 	for (uint32_t s = 1; s <= mp_last_step; s++) {
 		pandora_step = s;
-		if (mp_attach && s >= 4 && s <= 8) {
+		if (mp_attach && ((s >= 4 && s <= 6) || s == 8)) {
 			printf("PANDORA MPSS: step %u skipped (attach mode: no firmware is loaded or reset)\n", s);
 			continue;
 		}
